## Conventions

- Git: gitflow branch names (`feature/`, `fix/`, `hotfix/`, `release/`,
  `chore/`, `docs/`, `refactor/`, `test/`), squash merge to `main`, releases are
  annotated `vX.Y.Z` tags; a `release/X.Y.Z` branch only prepares one and is
  deleted after merging.
- Commits and pull request titles: Conventional Commits in English, one line,
  imperative mood. CI checks the pull request title.
- Code, comments and documentation are in English.
- Documentation diagrams use Mermaid and carry a short prose description.
- The changelog changes only when preparing a release.
- Decisions that close an alternative are recorded in `{{docs/adr}}/`.
  Records are immutable once merged to `main`: a changed decision is a new
  record that supersedes the old one, which changes only in its status line.

## Workflow

- Issues carry acceptance criteria as `WHEN ... THEN ...`, numbered `AC-n`.
  Tests that prove a criterion carry its identifier in their name.
